a)    the above-noted staff report BE RECEIVED; 



b)    the implementation of a Heritage Property Tax Relief Program BE REFERRED for consideration as part of the 2027-2031 Strategic Plan and 2028-2031 Multi-Year Budget process; and, 



c)    the Civic Administration BE DIRECTED to include, as part of the referral to the Multi Year Budget, a proposed structure or format based on the model used by the Town of Collingwood; 



it being noted that the Planning and Environment Committee received the following communication with respect to this matter: 



-    a communication dated September 17, 2026, from L. Claro.

That notwithstanding the recommendation of the Director, Planning and Development, the staff report dated September 21, 2026, related to the Designation Under Part IV of the Ontario Heritage Act for the Heritage Listed Property at 203 Bathurst Street BE RECEIVED for information and no further action be taken;



it being noted that the Planning and Environment Committee received the following communication with respect to this matter: 



-    a communication dated July 30, 2026, from S. Adams, City Storage Group; 



it being noted that the delegation request from T. Lundy, City Storage Group, with respect to this matter, was received.

That the following actions be taken with respect to the 9th Report of the Community Advisory Committee on Planning, from the meeting held on September 17, 2026:



a)     the City Clerk BE REQUESTED to revise the Community Advisory Committee on Planning (CACP) Terms of Reference to:



i) remove the requirement that all votes at the CACP be recorded votes; and,

ii) revise the Terms of Reference for the CACP to record the votes of all the members in attendance on the committee report if a recorded vote is requested for an agenda item;



b)    clauses 1.1, 3.1, 3.3-3.4, 4.1, 5.1-5.10 BE RECEIVED; 



it being noted that the delegation request from J.M. Metrailler, Chair, Community Advisory Committee on Planning, with respect to this matter, was received.
